  { q: 'Do ravens steal shiny objects?', a: 'The claim that ravens (and corvids in general) are strongly attracted to and steal shiny objects is a popular belief but is not supported by controlled experimental evidence. A 2014 study by Shephard et al. (University of Exeter) tested magpies — the bird most associated with this belief — and found they showed no preference for shiny objects, and were actually more cautious around novel shiny items. Ravens do manipulate and cache objects, but attraction to shininess specifically has not been demonstrated experimentally.' },
];
---

